\ A module-private mutable value-keyed map reachable at freeze time is carried into the
\ runtime-image AOT binary and reconstructed by the loader, matching the interpreter. The cache is
\ empty at freeze and routes through the mutable-value-map slot table: the parse-time-folded
\ binding becomes a mutable_value_map_slot push, and the loader allocates one live map per slot so
\ every call to `(cache)` shares the same backing. Runtime mutation through that shared backing
\ must persist across calls -- the persistence is what requires a slot, not a fresh value per push.
\
\ A fixnum key is the case `hash` and `mutable-map` cannot express at all.

(cache): ( -- mvmap ) <mutable-value-map> ;

remember: ( key value -- ) [ (cache) -rot> vmap-set! drop ] ;
recall:   ( key -- value ) [ (cache) swap vmap-get ] ;
known?:   ( key -- ? )     [ (cache) swap vmap-has? ] ;
tally:    ( -- n )         [ (cache) #len ] ;

1 known? .  \ f  -- empty at freeze
1 "one" remember
1 recall print-line  \ one -- runtime mutation persisted through the shared backing
{ 2 3 } "pair" remember
{ 2 3 } recall print-line  \ pair -- an array key matches by its frozen form
tally .                    \ 2
